# Auto-deploy to impacts after updates

**We deploy only to the Vercel project "impacts".** Do not use or reference any Vercel project named "impacts-web-app".

**Every time we make an update, the app should automatically deploy to impacts.** To make that happen:

1. **Commit** the changed files with a clear, short message (e.g. `Mentor dashboard: hospital cards, PECC info, activity list`).
2. **Push** to `origin main`: `git push origin main`.

With the GitHub repo connected to the Vercel project **impacts**, a push to `main` triggers an automatic production deploy. No need to run `vercel` manually unless you are testing a one-off deploy from the CLI.

Do this at the end of every code-change task unless the user says not to push or to hold off.
